Third-party Content

The native addon statically links the Lean 4 runtime and standard library
(Apache License 2.0, https://github.com/leanprover/lean4); the runtime is
rebuilt from the Lean v4.35.0 sources without GMP (Lean's built-in big-number
implementation, scripts/build_runtime_nogmp.sh) and contains mimalloc (MIT,
https://github.com/microsoft/mimalloc). It also statically links libuv (MIT,
https://github.com/libuv/libuv) as shipped with the Lean toolchain.

The WebAssembly build contains the Lean 4 runtime and standard library
(Apache License 2.0), compiled from the same sources without GMP, and the
mimalloc allocator of emscripten (MIT).

This package contains no GMP and no other LGPL-licensed code
(docs/gmp-licensing.md in the elk-lean repository).

